# Base URL of the ranking backend (no trailing slash).
# This is PUBLIC configuration: VITE_* variables are exposed to the browser,
# so never put secrets (API keys, passwords, tokens) here.
#
# Production/API deployment URL (documentation placeholder — not a real host):
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.example.com
#
# A local (untracked, ignored) frontend/.env may hold the real deployment URL
# for convenience (public, safe). `vite dev` still uses the local backend:
# the tracked frontend/.env.development pins VITE_API_BASE_URL to empty in
# development mode (it beats frontend/.env), so the browser calls relative
# `/api/...`, which the Vite dev proxy forwards to the local backend (see
# vite.config.js, default http://localhost:3001). A personal
# frontend/.env.local override is optional and also untracked.
# Deployed environments (e.g. Vercel Preview and Production) provide the real
# VITE_API_BASE_URL as an environment variable, which always takes precedence
# over any file. To build locally against a deployed backend instead, either
# set the OS environment variable for one command or temporarily move
# frontend/.env.local aside — never commit a real hostname.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.example.com
